analysisWe need to produce an assert statement for the comment.

We have method pop(): precondition: stack not empty (size >0). The comment: "If the stack is initially not empty, then the result is either null and the last item in the stack is null, or the result is equal to the last item in the stack."

Interpretation: For a non-empty stack before pop, after pop we return either null (if the last item was null) OR the result equals the last item before removal. Since removal also removes it, but we need to refer to old state. So assertion: \old(this.size()) > 0 => (\result == null && \old(this.get(this.size())) == null) || (\result.equals(\old(this.get(this.size())))). Wait after removal, size decreased by 1. Old size = n. After pop, new size = n-1. The last index before removal is n-1. After removal, size is n-1, so the old last item is at index n-1 before removal. In new state, that index no longer exists. So we need to refer to old get(n-1). Use \old(this.get(\old(this.size())-1)). The result is either null and that old element is null, or result equals that old element.

Thus assert: \old(this.size()) > 0 => ( (\result == null && \old(this.get(\old(this.size())-1)) == null) || (\result != null && \result.equals(\old(this.get(\old(this.size())-1))) ) );

But we could also write result == \old(this.get(\old(this.size())-1)). However if both null, equals would cause NullPointer. So need case distinction.

Simplify: \old(this.size()) > 0 => (\result == null ? \old(this.get(\old(this.size())-1)) == null : \result.equals(\old(this.get(\old(this.size())-1)))).

But we need to use logical operators. Use: (\result == null && \old(this.get(\old(this.size())-1)) == null) || (\result != null && \result.equals(\old(this.get(\old(this.size())-1)))).

Thus final assert.

Make sure to include parentheses for implication: \old(this.size()) > 0 => ( ... );

Return as code block.

